Feature: Presets written for kinds of record sit where those records' stems do
  Some presets are written for a kind of record rather than a room: a piano or celesta heard
  through the tape machine after the microphones, on lo-fi home records. The song corpus holds the
  user's own records of two kinds (14 lo-fi Guided by Voices tracks, 12 Olivia Tremor Control
  tracks), separated with htdemucs_6s, and measured by its scripts/features.py;
  tests/record_reference.hpp holds the quartiles of the piano and other stems (numbers only),
  generated by tools/record_gate_profiles.py. tests/record_features.hpp measures exactly as
  features.py does, pYIN wobble included, checked against it on every gated render with
  tools/record_gate_try.cpp (agreement to the printed digit).

  Executable: tests/record_gate_tests.cpp (CTest record_gate_tests).

  # each_records_preset_sits_inside_the_records_quartiles
  Scenario: Each records preset sits inside the records' quartiles
    Given each preset written for a kind of record, playing sixteen seconds of its phrase at 120 BPM
      | preset                       | records          | stem         | phrase |
      | Upright, four-track cassette | lo-fi GBV        | piano        | chords |
      | Upright, home studio tape    | OTC              | piano        | chords |
      | Celesta, home studio tape    | OTC              | piano, other | melody |
    Then its spectral centroid, 85% roll-off, share above 3 kHz, 100 ms crest, L/R correlation and pYIN tape wobble each land inside the interquartile range of that stem across those records
